# OAuth account center — frontend env example (LOCAL DEV against the infra dev stack).
#
# Copy to `.env` (this dir) and run `pnpm dev` (Nuxt dev server on :9420). Every
# var has a code-level fallback in `nuxt.config.ts`; the public API bases already
# default to the dev stack's oauth service on :9277, so the only value worth
# overriding for local work is the image CDN base (below). Production MUST set them.
# See docs/dev-environment.md.
#
# `NUXT_PUBLIC_*` / `KUN_VISUAL_NOVEL_NUXT_PUBLIC_*` become client-readable via
# `useRuntimeConfig().public.*` — DO NOT put secrets here.

# OAuth backend REST base (browser) — dev stack oauth service on :9277.
KUN_VISUAL_NOVEL_NUXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:9277/api/v1

# image_service CDN base (no trailing slash) → the dev stack's read-through proxy
# (:9290), which serves the <aa>/<bb>/<hash>.webp tree from local MinIO and falls
# back to the prod public CDN on a miss.
KUN_VISUAL_NOVEL_NUXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_CDN_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:9290

# Catalog + Trust + AI admin panels reach their services through same-origin
# Nitro relays (/catalog-proxy, /trust-proxy, /ai-proxy) that forward to the
# *_API_BASE_SSR values below. The defaults already work in local dev (the relay
# falls back to 127.0.0.1:9281 / :9283 / :9284), so these normally stay unset.
# KUN_VISUAL_NOVEL_NUXT_PUBLIC_CATALOG_API_BASE=/catalog-proxy
# KUN_VISUAL_NOVEL_NUXT_PUBLIC_TRUST_API_BASE=/trust-proxy
# KUN_VISUAL_NOVEL_NUXT_PUBLIC_AI_API_BASE=/ai-proxy

# SSR-side (in-container) service bases — set these only when running the Nuxt app
# inside docker (compose service names). Empty in local dev → the dual-base readers
# fall back to the public bases above.
# NUXT_API_BASE_SSR=http://oauth:9277/api/v1
# NUXT_CATALOG_API_BASE_SSR=http://catalog:9281/api/v1
# NUXT_TRUST_API_BASE_SSR=http://trust:9283/api/v1
# NUXT_AI_API_BASE_SSR=http://ai:9284/api/v1
